It seems to me that this kind of construct would make most if not elidable
terminators basically unneccesary. I could be wrong on that, and I'm not
stating a desire for that to happen.

In any case, if there are cases where "vau FA" isn't enough, I think it
would make most sense to alter the grammar of {vau} so that it /is/ enough,
rather than creating another word. I don't personally think using {cu} in
that respect is a good idea, but I do like the idea of having a word that
does as Robin proposes.


